<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">C. R. Swart</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1894–1982</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Charles Robberts Swart</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">C. R. Swart was a South African <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-party-south-africa">National Party</a> politician who served as minister of justice from 1948 to 1959, governor-general from 1960 and, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> became a republic on 31 May 1961, its first state president until 1967. As justice minister he introduced key security laws of early apartheid, including the Suppression of Communism Act of 1950.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/c-r-swart.jpg" alt="C. R. Swart" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ons eerste halfeeu 1910-1960 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CR_Swart_1960.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
